##### Barriers modulo permutation.

To consider whether training instability causes networks to converge to different permuted versions of the same loss basin, we apply the weight and activation matching algorithms from [Ainsworth et al. 2023](https://ar5iv.labs.arxiv.org/html/2506.13234#bib.bib2) to find a permutation of neurons PP that approximately minimizes the L2L^{2} distance between two networks’ weights or intermediate activations, respectively. To measure the degree to which θT\theta\_{T} and θT′\theta^{\prime}\_{T} have been permuted with respect to each other, we record both the barrier between θT\theta\_{T} and P⁡[θT′]P[\theta^{\prime}\_{T}], and the fraction of identity elements (unpermuted neurons) in PP.

